  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is clearly the dominant modality (best RNA-only: 0.650 vs best image-only: 0.208), and within RNA-only, multiprofile+avgpool+scvi_n200 (config_005, 0.650) is the current best. The RNA encoder choice is a critical, underexplored design axis: we've only tested pca_n2000 and scvi_n200. scgpt is a fundamentally different (generative, pretrained) encoder that could capture richer biological structure. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 when all other variables are held at their known-best settings (multiprofile, avgpool)? Why this is the best next experiment: It directly tests the most impactful remaining RNA-only design decision with a clean single-variable comparison against config_005. The result will determine which RNA encoder to anchor all future multimodal experiments on, making it high-value for the limited budget. Testing aggregation (config_006) is lower priority since avgpool already showed a large margin over transformer (0.591 vs 0.519), and multimodal configs are premature before establishing the best RNA backbone."
}

